TgyMTk=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:editor","name":"topic:editor","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":3240950060,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzMjQwOTUwMDYw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/performance","name":"performance","color":"447777","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2025-08-07T08:42:05Z","updated_at":"2025-11-24T15:30:27Z","closed_at":"2025-11-24T15:30:23Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nReproducible with\n- v4.5.beta5.mono.official [c81fd6c51]\n- v4.4.stable.mono.official [4c311cbee]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.5.beta5.mono - Windows 11 (build 26100) - Multi-window, 1 monitor - Vulkan (Forward+) - dedicated AMD Radeon RX 9060 XT (Advanced Micro Devices, Inc.; 32.0.21025.1024) - AMD Ryzen 7 9700X 8-Core Processor (16 threads) - 31.12 GiB memory, AMD driver version 25.8.1\n\n### Issue description\n\nI get a lot of stuttering when the game is run from Godot editor. This happen even in an empty project (well, I do have one label showing fps, but stuttering happens without the label too).\n\nMy computer is fast enough to run with 2000+ fps when vsync is disabled, so stuttering does not happen because of lacking hardware performance.\n\nStuttering happens when:\n- game is run from editor and Forward+ renderer is used\n\nStuttering does NOT happen when:\n- running exported game (using Forward+)\n- either profiler or visual profiler is running (using Forward+)\n- Compatibility renderer is used instead of Forward+\n\nFollowing is a screen shot from a stuttering run. FPS changes between 60 and 54.\n\n<img width=\"1084\" height=\"659\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2195a3e1-6240-4969-82b8-b7213b7755ab\" />\n\n\nFollowing is a screen shot from a non stuttering run where profiler is running. FPS stays at 60.\n\n<img width=\"1084\" height=\"660\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d887982c-d188-4dc0-9f9a-20d16e3a6959\" />\n\nWhat have I tried:\n- Changing options from AMD's driver (version 25.8.1), mainly different vsync options, but without any effect. \n- Running game embedded or a separate window doesn't change anything either.\n- Changing rendered backend to \"d3d12\" doesn't help.\n\nStuttering didn't happen when I previously used this same computer without graphics card and only with the integrated GPU.\n\nApparently the profilers do something that makes the rendering behave better. My current \"fix\" is just to auto start the profiler.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nJust running an empty project does this.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nN/A","closed_by":{"login":"AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips","html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://a